  "title": "Jagadish Chandra Bose",
  "summary": "Born in 1858 in Mymensingh (now Bangladesh), he took a professorship at Presidency College in Calcutta, where he was paid less than British colleagues. In 1895 he demonstrated wireless transmission of microwave signals, later turned to plant biophysics, and in 1917 founded the Bose Research Institute in Calcutta. He died in 1937.",
